{title: This Is My Father's World}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
This [C]is my [G]Father's [C]world[**]
And [F]to my [C]listening [G]ears[**]
All [C]nature [Am]sings, and [G]round me [C]rings
The [F]music [G]of the [C]spheres[**]
This [C]is my [F]Father's [C]world[**]
I [F]rest me [G]in the [C]thought[**]
Of [G]rocks and [Am]trees, of [F]skies and [C]seas
His [F]hand the [G]wonders [C]wrought.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
This [C]is my [G]Father's [C]world[**]
The [F]birds their [C]carols [G]raise[**]
The [C]morning [Am]light, the [G]lily [C]white
De[F]clare their [G]Maker's [C]praise[**]
This [C]is my [F]Father's [C]world[**]
He [F]shines in [G]all that's [C]fair[**]
In the [G]rustling [Am]grass I [F]hear Him [C]pass
He [F]speaks to [G]me every[C]where.[**]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
This [C]is my [G]Father's [C]world[**]
O [F]let me [C]ne'er for[G]get[**]
That [C]though the [F]wrong seems [G]oft so [C]strong
God [F]is the [G]Ruler [C]yet[**]
This [C]is my [F]Father's [C]world[**]
Why [F]should my [G]heart be [C]sad?[**]
The [G]Lord is [Am]King: let the [F]heavens [C]ring!
God [F]reigns; let [G]earth be [C]glad![**]
{end_of_verse}
